WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:03.203
We are now standing
in front of the Mao Yisheng statue.

2
00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:07.841
We honor him here because
he is our first Ph.D. graduate from CMU.

3
00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:11.077
We also have more than
30 different public art pieces,

4
00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:13.680
just like those located all across campus.

5
00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:17.617
The building behind us right now
is called Porter and Baker Hall,

6
00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:21.921
which is home to the Dietrich
College of Humanities and Social Sciences.

7
00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:26.988
We position humanities at the intersection
between humanity and technology at CMU.

8
00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:32.627
This college specifically houses 70+
majors and minors with most majors

9
00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:36.870
completed within two years, which allows
students to be really flexible.

10
00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:40.373
We also encourage
experiential learning opportunities

11
00:00:40.573 --> 00:00:44.911
to gain hands on experiences,
including internships, research,

12
00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:48.481
study abroad, and also the Pittsburgh
Summer Internship program,

13
00:00:48.515 --> 00:00:51.184
double majors, dual degrees
and so much more.

14
00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:54.220
We also have programs like
the Washington Semester,

15
00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:59.192
an international study abroad experiences
that allow students to apply their learning

16
00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:02.929
to societal challenges and connect
with communities around the world.

17
00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:07.700
Personally, I study abroad in Paris
my last spring semester, which was

18
00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:12.038
a really, really easy application process,
but also a fun experience.

19
00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:14.240
So I always recommend this to anyone

20
00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.077
who is interested to really
consider study abroad here.

21
00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:20.380
Similarly to the health professions
program we mentioned earlier,

22
00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:24.918
we also have a pre-law program available
here, and another special program

23
00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:28.321
to also talk about here
is called Information Systems,

24
00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:32.792
or IS, which is a joint program
between Dietrich and the Heinz College,

25
00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:36.763
which was the graduate program
that we mentioned earlier here on campus.

26
00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:39.265
And with that, we'll
head over to our next stop.

